    "Happy Dussehra from TotalMarket! NSE and BSE are closed today for Vijayadashami and trading resumes on Wednesday. Today India celebrates Ram's victory over Ravan, but the story has a lesson for anyone who trades. In tradition Ravan was no fool. He is described as a great scholar of the Vedas, astrology, Ayurveda and music, and is credited with composing the Shiva Tandava Stotram. His ten heads are often read as the four Vedas and six Shastras: knowledge in abundance.",
    "Still, he lost everything, and not because he lacked information. He lost because of pride. His brother Vibhishan and his wife Mandodari both warned him to return Sita and make peace. He threw Vibhishan out instead. He laughed at an army of monkeys and bears, and a single messenger, Hanuman, set Lanka on fire. Every trader will recognise this pattern: a smart person with a strong view who stops listening, refuses to admit a mistake and keeps adding to a losing position.",
    "Some ten heads are also said to stand for ego, anger, greed, desire and jealousy, the same emotions that drive overtrading and revenge trades. One popular retelling says that as Ravan lay dying, Lakshman went to learn from him. Ravan's advice: act on good intentions without delay, never look down on anyone, and keep your private matters to yourself. Put in trading terms: follow your plan without hesitating, respect the market and never underestimate risk, and do not let tips or chatter from others steer your decisions. This Dussehra, the effigy worth burning is the ego that will not take a small loss before it becomes a big one."
